      "problem": "$\\frac{4a+10b-12c}{8}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4a+10b-12c}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{4a}{8}+\\frac{10b}{8}-\\frac{12c}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{8}\\cdot a+\\frac{10}{8}\\cdot b-\\frac{12}{8}\\cdot c & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot a+\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot b-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot c & = \\\\ \\frac{a}{2}+\\frac{5b}{4}-\\frac{3c}{2} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
